WEBVTT

00:03:29.288 --> 00:03:31.288
out of our community so easily,

00:03:31.329 --> 00:03:34.204
where not everyone has resources to share

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:38.288
nor could companies be expected
to have the same level of trust.

00:03:38.329 --> 00:03:42.621
Instead, an alternative
more business-like approach

00:03:42.663 --> 00:03:44.496
for accessing on-demand resources

00:03:44.538 --> 00:03:47.788
has been flourishing recently,
called “cloud computing”,

00:03:47.829 --> 00:03:51.704
which other communities are now exploiting
to analyze their bag data.

00:03:51.954 --> 00:03:54.371
It might seem paradoxical
for a place like CERN,

00:03:54.413 --> 00:03:55.996
a lab focused on the study

00:03:56.038 --> 00:03:59.288
of the unimaginably small
building blocks of matter,

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:02.579
to be the source of something
as big as big data.